            "kira_final": "The sanitization is complete. All sensitive API keys and credentials have been replaced with consistent placeholder values across the repository.\n\n## Summary of Changes\n\n### Files Modified:\n1. **`ray_processing/process.py`** - Replaced hardcoded AWS credentials\n2. **`ray_processing/ray_cluster.yaml`** - Replaced AWS credentials, GitHub token, and Hugging Face token\n3. **`rust_processing/tokshuf-rs/README.md`** - Replaced placeholder text with consistent placeholders\n\n### Placeholder Values Used (consistent across all files):\n| Original Value | Replaced With |\n|---|---|\n| `[KEY-REDIGIERT]` | `<your-aws-access-key-id>` |\n| `D4w8z9wKN1aVeT3BpQj6kIuN7wH8X0M9KfV5OqzF` | `<your-aws-secret-access-key>` |\n| `[KEY-REDIGIERT]` | `<your-github-token>` |\n| `[KEY-REDIGIERT]` | `<your-huggingface-token>` |\n| `[REDACTED: FILL IN WITH YOUR DATA]` | `<your-aws-access-key-id>`, `<your-aws-secret-access-key>`, `<your-aws-region>` |\n\n### Files Not Requiring Changes:\n- `README.md` - Already had empty placeholders (`export AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID=`)\n- `baselines/README.md` - Already had empty placeholders\n- `tools/commoncrawl/ray_config/cluster-west.yaml` - Already had empty placeholders\n- `tools/eval_expdb.py` - Uses environment variables (`os.getenv()`) without hardcoded values\n\nNo actual sensitive values remain in the repository. The placeholder values are consistent and ready for users to replace with their own credentials.",
